window.DEVLOG.agents["d3_carsB"] = {"name": "Cars B: American muscle", "role": "Hand-built Mustang, Challenger, Hellcat widebody, Viper", "status": "done", "progress": 100, "current": "Polish done: Stallion pushed to a modern Mustang (tall forward-raked shark nose, high big trapezoid grille, long flat hood + dome, fastback C-pillar kick, haunches, tri-bars in a full-width black panel, 20in wheels, lower/wider stance, deck lip); Hellkat now clearly wider/meaner than Avenger (13cm riveted flares standing 7cm proud, carbon skirts, deep carbon splitter + end plates, black mouth bezel, air-catcher, bigger bulge/scoop/extractors, 2.06m wide, 1.69/1.71 track). Body tris: muscle 50.6k, brick 55.5k, widebody 59.9k, super 52.7k. tsc clean.", "done": ["_helpersB.ts: keyframed body loft (wheel arches, rounded+raked capped ends, panel split hood/trunk/body), greenhouse loft (glass/pillar/roof regions), axis Projector + conformal patches (lamps, grilles, vents, plates), shut-line ribbons, sweeps, liners, mirrors, interior, mergeByMaterial", "muscle Stallion: 47k tris, ~90 draw calls (one-line fastback + long quarter glass, shark nose + big trapezoid grille, tri-slash DRL lamps, power dome + vents, broad haunches, tri-bar tails, quad-exit diffuser)", "brick Avenger: 58k (recessed mouth + quad halo lamps under a hood lip, power bulge + scoop, scallop, thick C-pillar, racetrack tail ring, racing fuel cap on the right)", "widebody Hellkat: 59k (riveted bolt-on flares + swollen fenders, air-catcher inner-left lamp, airgrabber scoop + twin extractors, carbon splitter + rockers, quad tips, wider track)", "super Viperion: 51k (clamshell hood between fender humps with central bulge, twin vents, nose vent + fender louvres, gills, double-bubble roof + bubble hatch, sill side-exits with heat shields, snake-eye lamps, scaled tails, ACR splitter/canards/diffuser)", "own viewer dev/carsB.html"], "todo": [], "notes": "Exhaust anchors: Stallion 4 rear tips, Avenger 2, Hellkat 4, Viperion 4 SIDE exits in the sills (dir (-0.3,0,+-1)). paintMeshes = [hood, body(merged)]. body.userData {belt, sill, door, cowl}. Shared Look materials via import.meta.glob with fallbacks; switchable head/tail mats are per-car.", "etaMinutes": 0, "updated": "2026-10-24T07:46:12Z"};
